    <string name="phase_menstrual_desc">Uterine lining sheds. Rest and stay warm.</string>
    <string name="phase_follicular_desc">Body prepares for ovulation. Energy rises.</string>
    <string name="phase_ovulation_desc">Egg is released. Peak fertility window.</string>
    <string name="phase_luteal_desc">Post-ovulation. PMS symptoms may appear.</string>
    <string name="phase_menstrual_desc_day1">Day 1 — flow is often heaviest. Rest, stay warm, take it easy.</string>
    <string name="phase_menstrual_desc_day2">Day 2 — cramps may peak. A heat pad and gentle stretches can help.</string>
    <string name="phase_menstrual_desc_day3">Day 3 — flow is easing. Sip warm fluids and don\'t overdo it.</string>
    <string name="phase_menstrual_desc_day4">Day 4 — energy is returning. Iron-rich meals support recovery.</string>
    <string name="phase_menstrual_desc_day5_plus">Tail end — light spotting is normal. Listen to your body.</string>
    <string name="phase_follicular_desc_early">Early follicular — energy is bouncing back. Good time to start something new.</string>
    <string name="phase_follicular_desc_mid">Mid follicular — clear-headed and productive. Make the most of it.</string>
    <string name="phase_follicular_desc_late">Late follicular — fertile window is approaching. Cervical mucus may increase.</string>
    <string name="phase_ovulation_desc_early">Fertile window opening — chances of conception begin to rise.</string>
    <string name="phase_ovulation_desc_mid">Peak fertility — most likely to conceive now.</string>
    <string name="phase_ovulation_desc_late">Fertility waning — the window is closing soon.</string>
    <string name="phase_luteal_desc_early">Early luteal — calm and steady. Subtle PMS symptoms may begin.</string>
    <string name="phase_luteal_desc_mid">Mid luteal — mood swings or cravings are common. Be gentle with yourself.</string>
    <string name="phase_luteal_desc_late">Late luteal — period is near. Rest, hydrate, ease up on stressors.</string>
